Clip caption search results: [{'id': 'clip_0_37', 'text': 'The video features a host from SciShow (identifiable by the green logo in the bottom right corner) standing against a solid blue background. He is a bald man with a beard wearing a grey short-sleeved button-up shirt patterned with pink flamingos.\n\nAt the start (00:00), he speaks while gesturing with his hands. The scene cuts to a CGI rendering of a majestic white unicorn rearing on its hind legs against a golden, cloudy sky (00:02). \n\nThe video returns to the host (00:09), then transitions to a fantasy landscape (00:11) showing a flock of orange-brown dragons flying in formation over dark, jagged mountains shrouded in thick clouds or mist, with a sunset glowing in the background.\n\nCutting back to the host (00:19), he puts on a white plush unicorn headband featuring ears and a spiral horn (00:21). Wearing the headband, he continues speaking animatedly, using expressive hand gestures and occasionally adjusting the headband or pointing to the horn (00:22-00:36).\n\nThe mood is educational yet playful and lighthearted, shifting to humorous when the host dons the whimsical unicorn headband. No text appears on screen beyond the SciShow logo.', 'similarity score': 0.7472047805786133, 'start': 0.0, 'end': 37.037}, {'id': 'clip_157_277', 'text': 'In this SciShow clip, a bald, bearded host in a grey button-down shirt with pink flamingo patterns stands against a blue background and explains the evolutionary biology behind why no animals have evolved a single central horn (like unicorns).\n\n**Key moments and visuals:**\n\n- **00:00-00:23:** The host gestures while explaining that while animals have evolved various weapons like teeth, claws, and horns, no species has developed exactly one central horn.\n- **00:23:** A close-up photograph of a goat with horizontal rectangular pupils appears, illustrating the host\'s point about headgear location.\n- **00:28:** White text appears on screen stating: *"There are no pe