nary specialization of these cells in pecorans.\n\n**01:45-01:58:** Text appears on the left side of the screen reading: *"Until we see it happen to the genes that do get passed down, we aren\'t going to get any deer-icorns."* The host explains why animals don\'t have both horns and antlers. As he mentions horses and cows, images of a rearing horse (top left) and a cow\'s head (top right) briefly appear beside him.\n\n**Mood:** The tone is informative and accessible, using scientific diagrams, wildlife photography, and light humor to explain complex evolutionary biology concepts.', 'similarity score': 0.5759395360946655, 'start': 277.03700000000003, 'end': 397.03700000000003}]
